(Executive Summary) Tj
T*
(In the start of September 2018, the Sila Foundation contracted NCC Group to perform a review of) Tj
T*
(the Clef command-line interface. The Clef CLI is a selfcontained account management tool that can also be) Tj
T*
(used as a ?signing server? to auto-approve transactions) Tj
T*
(and other available methods of an API exposed through) Tj
T*
(various interfaces. One consultant was tasked to look) Tj
T*
(for usability and security issues with the tool and its API.) Tj
T*
(One extra consultant was added to the project at no extra cost to the Sila Foundation. A discord channel) Tj
T*
(was used to communicate with the development team.) Tj
T*
(Some medium-risk issues were discovered while a few) Tj
T*
(observations and recommendations were written up.) Tj
T*
(No major issues were found.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Scope) Tj
T*
(Commit 70cfedc9d7bd64f1f112eb2099a5c36266863f4) Tj
T*
(0 of Clef was audited, the scope included the following) Tj
T*
(items:) Tj
T*
(Clef. The Sila Foundation has developed a selfcontained tool for account management. It can be used) Tj
T*
(to create accounts, list them, sign transactions, sign) Tj
T*
(arbitrary data and recover public keys from signatures.) Tj
T*
(It can be used as a simple command-line interface \(CLI\)) Tj
T*
(or with a graphical user interface \(GUI\). Requests are) Tj
T*
(made through an API exposed via an IPC or a JSON-RPC) Tj
T*
(interface. Clef can also be used with different types of) Tj
T*
(?backends?, from simple file system wallets to hardware) Tj
T*
(wallets like the Trezor 1 and the Nano Ledger.2) Tj
T*
(Rules. Clef supports automation of requests handling,) Tj
T*
(allowing users to develop Javascript functions that will) Tj
T*
(approve or reject requests to the API based on time,) Tj
T*
(the Clef state and the request being made. This allows) Tj
T*
(Clef to run without user-interaction \(although it will be) Tj
T*
(required as a fallback if the functions written fail to) Tj
T*
(correctly approve or reject requests\).) Tj
T*
(The following items were not included in scope:) Tj
T*
(Crypto.) Tj
T*
(Clef relies on a couple of cryptographic) Tj
T*
(primitives which are not part of the standard go library:) Tj
T*
(keccak256 \(a variant of SHA-3\) and secp256k1 \(for the) Tj
T*
(ECDSA signature algorithm and recovering public keys) Tj
T*
(out of such signatures\).) Tj
T*
(Accounts. Clef relies heavily on the accounts package) Tj
T*
(of go-sila for parsing a transaction?s call data via) Tj
T*
(accounts/abi, for managing accounts via accounts/) Tj
T*
(keystore and for compatibility with hardware wallets) Tj
T*
(1) Tj
T*
(2) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(via accounts/usbwallet.) Tj
T*
(While a full review of) Tj
T*
(these packages was not in scope, the consultants) Tj
T*
(have partially reviewed them when relevant to the Clef) Tj
T*
(application.) Tj
T*
(BigNumber.js. Javascript rules written for Clef can make) Tj
T*
(use of this extra dependency for handling big numbers.) Tj
T*
(This library is a single file of less than 3000 lines of code) Tj
T*
(and was not audited as part of this engagement.) Tj
T*
(Otto. Otto is a Javascript interpreter written in Go used) Tj
