T*
(The Clef CLI can be used to create and manage Sila externally owned accounts. The) Tj
T*
(account creation process can be started by sending the following RPC request to Clef \(if run) Tj
T*
(with the --rpc option\):) Tj
T*
(curl -H "Content-Type: application/json" -X POST --data '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","metho) Tj
T*
(d":"account_new","params":["test"],"id":67}' localhost:8550) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The user running the Clef process is then prompted to enter a password which is used to) Tj
T*
(protect the account?s private key. At this point the user can enter an arbitrary-length password \(empty) Tj
T*
(passwords are also accepted\). This would facilitate recovery of the accounts?s) Tj
T*
(private keys to attackers physically or remotely breaching the device where Clef is installed.) Tj
T*
(Recommendation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Enforce a minimum password length. The NIST organization has published documents 5) Tj
T*
(about the topic, recommending to set a minimum-length of 8 characters for such passwords.) Tj
T*
(Additionally, check for known bad passwords. Various lists of known bad passwords like the) Tj
T*
(NBP 6 exist.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Client Response) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
