(A maliciously crafted data field could allow an attacker to deceive the signer?s intent.) Tj
T*
(When receiving a request to sign a transaction, Clef first attempts to perform a few validation) Tj
T*
(checks before passing the request to the user. If a special argument is passed to the request) Tj
T*
(\(a method?s signature\) the program also attempts to match it against the data field. In that) Tj
T*
(case, the data field must be composed of a 4-byte identifier for the function called \(which is) Tj
T*
(the hash of the method?s signature truncated to 4 bytes\) and a multiple of 32 bytes:) Tj
T*
(func parseCallData\(calldata []byte, abidata string\) \(*decodedCallData, error\) {) Tj
T*
(if len\(calldata\) < 4 {) Tj
T*
(return nil, fmt.Errorf\("Invalid ABI-data, incomplete method sign) Tj
T*
