T*
(Clef allow users to write rules \(in javascript\) in order to automate handling of the requests) Tj
T*
(to Clef. Several examples are given in the documentation,13 the first one being a time rule) Tj
T*
(limiting how much ether can be sent over a window of 1 week. For this, the javascript run-time) Tj
T*
(environment relies on the time given by the system:) Tj
T*
(var windowstart = new Date\(\).getTime\(\) - window;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(There exist different ways for attackers to affect the time of the device running Clef without) Tj
T*
(being root on the system:) Tj
T*
(1. If the CAP_SYS_TIME capability 14 is set on the date program, any user can change the) Tj
T*
(time.) Tj
T*
(2. If the attacker has a privileged man-in-the-middle position in the network, she could attack) Tj
T*
(the NTP protocol 15 to alter the device?s time.) Tj
T*
(Furthermore, to keep a state in between executions of the rules, Clef keeps an encrypted keyvalue storage) Tj
T*
( \(jsStorage\). Particular attacks might allow an attacker to alter this state and) Tj
T*
(remove some limitations \(for example if a boolean has ben set to prevent further transactions,) Tj
T*
(reverting the state would allow transactions to flow again\):) Tj
T*
(1. If the attacker has a physical access to the machine, she could re-set it to a previous) Tj
T*
(snapshot.) Tj
T*
(2. If the attacker has file permissions to the jsStorage, she could record changes and revert) Tj
T*
(the file to a previous point in time.) Tj
T*
(These attacks could allow an attacker to prevent certain rules from working correctly, or) Tj
T*
(worse, to drain wallets if the attacker has direct access to Clef?s API.) Tj
T*
(Recommendation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This finding highlights the fact that the security of the system running Clef is of utmost) Tj
T*
(importance. Different type of users should be given different recommendations, depending) Tj
T*
(on how much is at stake. Different threat models could be written, documenting what Clef) Tj
T*
(protects against and does not protect against. Ultimately, it is hard to defend against these) Tj
T*
(types of highly targeted attacks from powerful adversaries, and they should be out of the) Tj
T*
(threat model of Clef.) Tj
