(Description) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clef?s API exposes an ?Import? method allowing requests to import already existing accounts.) Tj
T*
(This import method accepts an encrypted key as argument, which must be formatted under) Tj
T*
(specific formats. Two formats are accepted by Clef: a version 1 and a version 3, which utilize) Tj
T*
(different encryption methods. Most of the code following the import of the key systematically) Tj
T*
(assumes that the argument passed by the request is trusted, which might be in practice since) Tj
T*
(rules cannot be written to handle this method: the user must manually accept an import) Tj
T*
(request. The following code paths all have issues:) Tj
T*
(Importing Private Keys. The Import flow ends up calling the crypto.ToECDSAUnsafe\(\)) Tj
T*
(method which, as indicated, ?blindly converts a binary blob to a private key. It should almost) Tj
T*
(never be used unless you are sure the input is valid and want to avoid hitting errors due to) Tj
T*
(bad origin encoding \(0 prefixes cut off\).?) Tj
T*
(JSON Parsing. Several fields from the passed JSON object are retrieved without previously) Tj
T*
(checking if they exist. The getKDFKey\(\) function used to retrieve KDF parameters from the) Tj
T*
(request does not expect an empty map as cryptoJSON.KDFParams and will crash if given) Tj
T*
(one. Additionally, it expects integers as fields for the KDF object, even when given strings.) Tj
T*
(KDF parameters. A denial of service can be obtained by providing absurdly large parameters for the Scrypt) Tj
T*
( Key Derivation Function, which will force the program to compute an) Tj
T*
(interminable cryptographic operation.) Tj
T*
(Authenticated Encryption. Before attempting the decryption of the imported key, the keystore will verify) Tj
T*
(the integrity of the ciphertext in order to detect any tampering from man-inthe-middle attackers. This) Tj
T*
(integrity check does not include the IV and is not done in constant) Tj
T*
(time. This could allow an attacker to tamper with the IV, making the user decrypt the wrong) Tj
T*
(private key, without any alert given by Clef \(even though the ?address? recovered is different) Tj
T*
(from the ?address? field passed as argument in the request\).) Tj
T*
(Decryption. Version 1 of the Importer will use AES-CBC to decrypt the received key, in) Tj
T*
(particular the low-level CryptBlocks function which takes a multiple of the blocksize as) Tj
T*
(argument. If not, the function will panic, as can be seen in .16) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Reproduction Steps) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
