() Tj
T*
(The keystore package of Go-Sila has an exported EncryptKey\(\) method capable of) Tj
T*
(storing wallets in an encrypted form. The encryption uses a key derived from a passphrase) Tj
T*
(known by the user. As a mean of integrity check, to ensure that a backup of an encrypted key) Tj
T*
(has not been tampered with, the keystore computes a message authentication code \(MAC\)) Tj
T*
(over the ciphertext as can be seen below:) Tj
T*
(// EncryptKey encrypts a key using the specified scrypt parameters into a json) Tj
T*
(// blob that can be decrypted later on.) Tj
T*
(func EncryptKey\(key *Key, auth string, scryptN, scryptP int\) \([]byte, error\) {) Tj
T*
(// ...) Tj
T*
(derivedKey, err := scrypt.Key\(authArray, salt, scryptN, scryptR, scrypt) Tj
T*
(P, scryptDKLen\)) Tj
T*
(// ...) Tj
T*
(iv := make\([]byte, aes.BlockSize\) // 16) Tj
T*
(if _, err := io.ReadFull\(rand.Reader, iv\); err != nil {) Tj
T*
(panic\("reading from crypto/rand failed: " + err.Error\(\)\)) Tj
T*
(}) Tj
T*
(cipherText, err := aesCTRXOR\(encryptKey, keyBytes, iv\)) Tj
T*
(// ...) Tj
T*
